---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# One tools.ask (or tools.secret) whose timeout, a Stop, or stdin's EOF
# races a late answer from the web. Recipe: go/tests/model/README.md.
# ask_answer.fizz treats "the ask resolves" (Resolve) and "serve delivers
# the answer" (Deliver) as atomic and exclusive; in the code they are
# five processes that only meet at a mutex or a pipe, and this spec
# keeps each step apart:
#
#   Asker     plugins/ask/ask.go putIn: select on done / ch / timeout.
#             The timeout and done branches delete pending[id] under mu
#             only AFTER the select chose them (Timeout/CancelByStop, then
#             GiveUp). Answer (ask.go Answer) takes pending[id] under mu,
#             appends ask/answer ("[secret stored]" for a secret) and
#             sends on the buffered ch. Cancel closes ch.
#   Headless  plugins/ui/headless.go: the event handler sets hlAsk on
#             "ask" and clears it on the call's end (askEnded) or
#             done/error (ChildEnd); the stdin reader hands a line to
#             hlAnswerPending while hlAsk is set, which on an Answer error
#             sets hlErrored and prints to stderr only (ReadLine); EOF
#             runs hlCancelAsk (StdinEOF).
#   Serve     internal/serve/supervisor.go Answer: PendingAsk, write the
#             line, disarm, 200 (ServeWrite); emitLocked disarms on the
#             end event the scanner reads (ScanEnd).
#   Page      app.tsx: shows the question while StatusOf over history
#             says it is open (Poll), POSTs /answer (UserAnswer); a
#             timed-out call reads "no answer after" (app.tsx:2259).
#   Keychain  ask.go secretVia: Store runs AFTER Answer wrote "[secret
#             stored]" (Store / StoreFails).
#
# Where the mapped model differed from the code (the code wins):
#   - The timeout and cancel are two steps each: the select's choice
#     (timeout_fired) and the delete under mu (GiveUp,
#     pending_deleted_after_timeout). CancelByStop's done branch is the
#     same two steps; Headless' Cancel (EOF) is one step under mu.
#   - hlAsk is cleared by the child's own handler of the end event
#     (ChildEnd), not by serve's scanner; serve disarms later (ScanEnd).
#     Between the two a POST is written and 200'd with no ask to take it
#     in the child: the line becomes a steer or a new turn
#     (lost == "steer"), not only the stderr loss the mapping named.
#   - The mapped state arm_still_set is the window ChildEnd..ScanEnd.
#   - "late_answer_409" is ServeWrite after ScanEnd (post == "refused").
#
# What the code does NOT keep, with fizz's counterexamples (each found by
# adding the claim as an assertion):
#   - "An ask resolves exactly one way": AskPlain, Timeout, UserAnswer,
#     ServeWrite, ReadLine (Answer takes the pending entry the timeout
#     branch has not deleted yet: history "You answered"), GiveUp. The
#     model got "no answer after", the transcript says answered.
#   - "History never says answered / secret stored for an ask whose tool
#     errored": AskSecret, UserAnswer, ServeWrite, ReadLine, Receive,
#     StoreFails ("[secret stored]" is written before the store).
#   - "A POST /answer reported ok was delivered to the ask it named":
#     AskPlain, Timeout, GiveUp, UserAnswer, ServeWrite (still armed:
#     200), ReadLine (hlAsk still set, Answer refuses: stderr). And
#     AskPlain, Timeout, GiveUp, ChildEnd, UserAnswer, ServeWrite (arm
#     still set), ReadLine (hlAsk nil: the answer steers the turn).
#   - "A lost answer is reported to the person": the same first path;
#     nothing in the code tells the page, hlErrored and stderr are all.
#   - Liveness "an answer lost does not end errored without the page
#     saying why": that path, then ChildEnd, ScanEnd, Poll, stuck.
# The claims below are what the code does keep, and they pin each loss
# to the exact window that causes it.
#
# Fields (Ask role):
#   kind     "" before the ask, "plain" (tools.ask) or "secret"
#   call     the blocked tool call: open | fired (select chose timeout or
#            done; pending not yet deleted) | got (a secret's value is
#            back, not yet stored) | answered (returned the answer) |
#            failed (returned an error)
#   pending  Asker.pending[id] exists
#   chan     the answer channel: "" | sent (Answer sent a value) | closed
#   hist     history has ask/answer (or "[secret stored]") for it
#   hlAsk    the child's headless hlAsk is set
#   end      the call's end: "" | out (recorded and on the child's stdout)
#            | seen (serve's scanner read it)
#   arm      serve's s.asks[id]
#   shown    the page shows the question (needs-you)
#   post     the page's POST /answer: "" | sent | ok (200) | refused
#   line     the answer line is in the child's stdin pipe, unread
#   eof      the child's stdin closed
#   errored  hlErrored
#   lost     an answer that did not reach its call: "" | unread (Answer
#            sent it after the select chose the timeout) | stderr (Answer
#            refused it: hlErrored + a stderr line) | steer (read with no
#            hlAsk: it went to the loop as a message)
#   stored   a secret was stored in the keychain

role Ask:
    action Init:
        self.kind = ""
        self.call = ""
        self.pending = False
        self.chan = ""
        self.hist = False
        self.hlAsk = False
        self.end = ""
        self.arm = False
        self.shown = False
        self.post = ""
        self.line = False
        self.eof = False
        self.errored = False
        self.lost = ""
        self.stored = False

    # The model calls tools.ask / tools.secret: pending, the ask event
    # (hlAsk in the child, then serve arms it), and the page shows it.
    # Folded into one step: ask_answer.fizz covers the arming.
    atomic action AskPlain:
        require self.kind == ""
        self.kind = "plain"
        self.open()

    atomic action AskSecret:
        require self.kind == ""
        self.kind = "secret"
        self.open()

    atomic func open():
        self.call = "open"
        self.pending = True
        self.hlAsk = True
        self.arm = True
        self.shown = True

    # The select chooses the timeout, or the run's done (Stop). Go picks
    # at random among ready cases, so it may choose them with an answer
    # already in ch.
    atomic fair action Timeout:
        require self.call == "open"
        self.call = "fired"

    atomic action CancelByStop:
        require self.call == "open"
        self.call = "fired"

    # The chosen branch deletes pending[id] and returns the error. An
    # answer Answer sent meanwhile stays in ch, never read.
    atomic fair action GiveUp:
        require self.call == "fired"
        self.pending = False
        self.call = "failed"
        if self.chan == "sent":
            self.lost = "unread"

    # The select takes ch: an answer, or the close Cancel made.
    atomic fair action Receive:
        require self.call == "open" and self.chan != ""
        if self.chan == "closed":
            self.call = "failed"
        elif self.kind == "secret":
            self.call = "got"
        else:
            self.call = "answered"

    # secretVia stores the value after Answer recorded "[secret stored]".
    atomic fair action Store:
        require self.call == "got"
        self.stored = True
        self.call = "answered"

    atomic action StoreFails:
        require self.call == "got"
        self.call = "failed"

    # The child's handler sees the call's end (askEnded, or the block's
    # result): clears hlAsk, the loop records it, it goes to stdout.
    atomic fair action ChildEnd:
        require self.end == "" and (self.call == "answered" or self.call == "failed")
        self.hlAsk = False
        self.end = "out"

    # serve's scanner reads it: emitLocked disarms.
    atomic fair action ScanEnd:
        require self.end == "out"
        self.end = "seen"
        self.arm = False

    # The page's poll: needs-you while history has the ask open (no
    # answer entry, no end) and its child is alive.
    atomic fair action Poll:
        require self.shown != (self.kind != "" and not self.hist and self.end == "" and not self.eof)
        self.shown = not self.shown

    # The person answers the question on screen (once per walk).
    atomic action UserAnswer:
        require self.shown and self.post == ""
        self.post = "sent"

    # supervisor.Answer: armed and the child's stdin open, so the line is
    # written, the arm dropped, and the POST 200'd; otherwise ErrNoAsk.
    atomic fair action ServeWrite:
        require self.post == "sent"
        if self.arm and not self.eof:
            self.line = True
            self.arm = False
            self.post = "ok"
        else:
            self.post = "refused"

    # The child's stdin reader takes the line (hlLineIn).
    atomic fair action ReadLine:
        require self.line
        self.line = False
        if not self.hlAsk:
            self.lost = "steer"
        else:
            self.hlAsk = False
            if self.pending:
                self.pending = False
                self.hist = True
                self.chan = "sent"
            else:
                self.errored = True
                self.lost = "stderr"

    # stdin closes (serve dropping the child, or a headless run's input
    # ending) after every line in the pipe was read. serve's drop
    # disarms; hlCancelAsk marks the run errored and Cancel closes ch.
    atomic action StdinEOF:
        require self.kind != "" and not self.eof and not self.line
        self.eof = True
        self.arm = False
        if self.hlAsk:
            self.hlAsk = False
            self.errored = True
            if self.pending:
                self.pending = False
                self.chan = "closed"

action Init:
    ask = Ask()

# The model got the answer only if history recorded it, and a secret's
# "answered" means the keychain has it.
always assertion AnsweredIsRecorded:
    return ask.call != "answered" or (ask.hist and (ask.kind != "secret" or ask.stored))

# History says answered while the call failed in exactly two ways: the
# select chose the timeout/Stop with the answer arriving (the Answer took
# the pending entry the timeout branch had not yet deleted), or the
# keychain store failed after "[secret stored]" was written.
always assertion AnsweredButFailedOnlyByTheRace:
    return not (ask.hist and ask.call == "failed") or ask.lost == "unread" or (ask.kind == "secret" and not ask.stored)

# A POST reported ok and read by the child reached its call, except in
# the three windows the code leaves open: the select already chose the
# timeout (unread), the call returned before the line was read (stderr),
# or the child's handler cleared hlAsk before serve's scanner disarmed
# (steer).
always assertion OkDeliveredOrLostInAWindow:
    return not (ask.post == "ok" and not ask.line) or ask.hist or ask.lost != ""

# hlErrored is set by EOF with the ask pending, or by an answer Answer
# refused; the stderr loss always sets it.
always assertion LostToStderrMarksErrored:
    return ask.lost != "stderr" or ask.errored

# A line is written only while armed with stdin open, and never twice.
always assertion OneLine:
    return not ask.line or (ask.post == "ok" and not ask.eof)

# The ask resolves: the call returns (timeout is fair), its end reaches
# serve, the arm, hlAsk and needs-you all clear.
always eventually assertion AskClears:
    return ask.kind == "" or not ask.arm and not ask.hlAsk and not ask.shown and ask.call != "open" and ask.call != "fired" and ask.call != "got"
